  },
  "localVerificationBeforeTransition": {
    "reviewedAt": "2026-10-30",
    "commands": [
      "node scripts/check-gorm-sql-literal.mjs -> exit 0, \"GORM SQL text and column names are literals or package constants across business modules\", 4 line-scoped waivers printed",
      "node --test tests/scripts/check-gorm-sql-literal.test.mjs -> 13 tests, 13 pass, 0 fail",
      "sed -n over all 18 sinks that were still open before this transition"
    ],
    "ciWiring": ".github/workflows/quality.yml steps \"Check GORM SQL literalness\" and \"Test GORM SQL literalness checker\" run npm run check:gorm-sql-literal / npm run test:gorm-sql-literal without continue-on-error, so a dynamic SQL argument reaching a GORM sink fails the required Quality Gates context instead of needing a manual re-review.",
    "sinkShapes": "the 18 remaining gosecurity:S3649 sinks are either Updates(map) calls whose map keys are assigned from quoted string literals in the same function (the checker rejects a non-literal key) or First(&model, id) primary-key lookups that GORM sends as bind parameters. No request value reaches SQL text at any of them."
  },
  "justifications": {
    "gosecurity:S3649": "False positive. Every SQL text or column-name argument reaching this sink is a source literal, a clause/gorm expression, or a package-level literal constant. That invariant is enforced in CI by scripts/check-gorm-sql-literal.mjs (package-wide declaration scan; reassigned variables, function parameters and request-derived values are excluded) and blocks in the \"Check GORM SQL literalness\" step of the docs-governance job in .github/workflows/quality.yml. Waivers are line-scoped, require a written justification and are printed in the job log. No request value reaches SQL text here.",
    "gosecurity:S2083": "False positive. The path handed to os.Remove is the result of resolveWithinRoot(storage.BasePath, filepath.Join(dateDir, unixSeconds + \"-\" + sanitizeUploadFileName(name))): the attacker-controlled multipart name is reduced to a single path element with both separators treated as directory parts, and the joined result is rejected unless it stays inside the storage root. That exact data flow is pinned by TestUploadPathStaysInsideRootForAdversarialNames, TestResolveWithinRootKeepsPathsInsideStorage and TestSanitizeUploadFileNameReducesNameToOneElement, all of which run in the Backend Tests CI job. SonarCloud accepted the same sanitizer for the os.Create call site in the 2026-10-30 analysis but does not carry it to the cleanup calls."
  },
